WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.085
India's rain comes with the monsoon.

2
00:00:02.285 --> 00:00:03.687
So why does Delhi get rain

3
00:00:03.687 --> 00:00:04.226
in winter?

4
00:00:04.726 --> 00:00:06.966
Blame a storm from the Mediterranean.

5
00:00:07.416 --> 00:00:08.974
A western disturbance is

6
00:00:08.974 --> 00:00:10.467
an extratropical storm,

7
00:00:10.587 --> 00:00:12.315
born over the Mediterranean

8
00:00:12.315 --> 00:00:13.275
or Caspian Sea.

9
00:00:13.675 --> 00:00:15.296
The westerlies carry it east,

10
00:00:15.396 --> 00:00:17.084
across Iran, Afghanistan

11
00:00:17.084 --> 00:00:17.999
and Pakistan,

12
00:00:18.099 --> 00:00:19.101
into India.

13
00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:20.952
When it meets the Himalayas,

14
00:00:21.052 --> 00:00:22.567
it brings rain to the plains

15
00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:24.288
and heavy snow to the hills.

16
00:00:24.688 --> 00:00:26.132
That winter rain matters

17
00:00:26.132 --> 00:00:27.035
for rabi crops.

18
00:00:27.285 --> 00:00:28.693
Too much can damage them,

19
00:00:28.793 --> 00:00:30.226
and bring landslides and

20
00:00:30.226 --> 00:00:30.883
avalanches.

21
00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:32.723
The monsoon is tropical,

22
00:00:32.723 --> 00:00:34.462
and carries its moisture low.

23
00:00:34.612 --> 00:00:36.100
A western disturbance carries

24
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:36.767
it higher up.

25
00:00:37.217 --> 00:00:38.326
Different storm.

26
00:00:38.526 --> 00:00:39.721
Different season.

27
00:00:40.221 --> 00:00:41.117
Your turn.

28
00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:42.987
Where do western disturbances

29
00:00:42.987 --> 00:00:43.529
come from?
